import string

def word_histogram(text):
    if not text:
        return {}
    text = text.lower()
    for char in string.punctuation:
        text = text.replace(char, '')
    words = text.split()
    histogram = {}
    for word in words:
        histogram[word] = histogram.get(word, 0) + 1
    return histogram
```

This function will convert the input string to lowercase, remove any punctuation, split it into words, and then count the frequency of each word using a dictionary.

